        terms: ['Lempel-Ziv', 'dictionary coding', 'universal code', 'source with memory', 'adaptive compression'],
        definition:
          'Lempel-Ziv coding builds a dictionary of previously seen phrases as it reads the source, encoding each new phrase as a pointer to the longest matching earlier phrase plus one new symbol. It requires no prior knowledge of the source statistics, which makes it universal: it approaches the entropy rate of any stationary ergodic source as the sequence length grows. Its decisive advantage over Huffman is that it exploits memory — repeated patterns become single pointers regardless of individual symbol probabilities — which is why it underlies gzip, PNG and the compress utility while Huffman appears mostly as a back-end.',
