        definition:
          'Channel capacity is C = max over p(x) of I(X;Y), the largest mutual information achievable by any choice of input distribution, measured in bits per channel use. The maximisation is over the transmitter design space, since the channel matrix itself is fixed by physics, and concavity guarantees a unique maximum. For symmetric channels the maximising distribution is uniform, which makes the calculation easy; for asymmetric channels it generally is not, and numerical methods are required. Capacity is a property of the channel alone, and it is the ceiling every coding scheme in the remaining modules is trying to approach.',
