        definition:
          'The generator matrix G is a k-by-n matrix whose rows form a basis for the code, so every codeword is c = mG where m is the k-bit message row vector and all arithmetic is modulo 2. Encoding is therefore one matrix multiplication, and the code is entirely determined by G. Different generator matrices related by row operations produce the same code with a different mapping from messages to codewords, which means G is not unique but the code it generates is. Reducing G to the systematic form [I_k | P] gives a mapping in which the message appears verbatim in the first k positions.',
