        definition:
          'The parity check matrix H is an (n-k)-by-n matrix whose null space is the code, so a vector c is a codeword if and only if cH transpose equals zero. Where G builds codewords, H tests them, and the two are related by G H transpose = 0. When G is in the systematic form [I_k | P], the parity check matrix follows immediately as H = [P transpose | I_(n-k)], which is why systematic form is worth reaching. H is the object the decoder actually uses, because the receiver does not know the message but can always apply the test.',
