        definition:
          'A code with minimum distance d_min detects any error pattern of up to d_min - 1 errors, because fewer than d_min changes cannot turn one codeword into another. It corrects up to t = floor((d_min - 1)/2) errors, because spheres of radius t around each codeword are disjoint when 2t < d_min, so a received word within t of a codeword is closer to that one than to any other. Detection and correction trade against each other: a code with d_min = 5 can correct two errors, or detect four while correcting none, or correct one while detecting three.',
