        definition:
          'Optimum decoding of a convolutional code means maximum likelihood sequence estimation: choosing the transmitted sequence, among all sequences the encoder could have produced, that maximises the likelihood of the received sequence. On a binary symmetric channel with crossover below one half, this reduces to choosing the trellis path at minimum Hamming distance from the received sequence; on a Gaussian channel with soft outputs, it becomes minimum Euclidean distance. Done naively this is a search over 2^L paths for an L-bit message, which is impossible for any useful L — and the whole content of the Viterbi algorithm is that the trellis structure makes the same answer reachable in linear time.',
